# Git SSH Allowed Signers (Cryptographic Provenance Trust Store)
# Platform : macOS (Apple Silicon arm64 Darwin 25+)
# Standard : OpenSSH PROTOCOL.sshsig / RFC 8308
# Target   : ~/.config/git/allowed_signers
# ==============================================================
#
# HOW TO CONFIGURE:
# 1. Copy this template to ~/.config/git/allowed_signers:
#      cp ~/.config/git/allowed_signers.example ~/.config/git/allowed_signers
#
# 2. Add your developer email and hardware-backed public key:
#      <email> namespaces="git" <key-type> <base64-public-key> [comment]
#
# Examples:
#
# Apple Secure Enclave / Secretive (NIST P-256):
# user@example.com namespaces="git" ecdsa-sha2-nistp256 AAAAE2VjZHNhLXNoYTItbmlzdHAyNTYAAAAIbmlzdHAyNTYAAABB... user@workstation
#
# FIDO2 / YubiKey (ecdsa-sk):
# user@example.com namespaces="git" sk-ecdsa-sha2-nistp256@openssh.com AAAAGnNrLWVjZHNhLXNoYTItbmlzdHAyNTZ... user@yubikey
